#: ../../source/docs/flightaxis.rst:5
#: 8a2e6264587944dfa478586b3d55138b
msgid "Understanding SITL with RealFlight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightaxis.rst:7
#: dbe83a4c7949449e8e0d1fc4656c77c5
msgid "This document will explain how SITL communicates with RealFlight for graphical simulations. In order to do any simulation you need several elements:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightaxis.rst:9
#: c899c59f20894a9baafd409a3d924b5e
msgid "A model of the vehicle, including its physical characteristics and their impacts on the physics model, control mechanisms, and a graphical data base of its appearance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightaxis.rst:11
#: f30fee8d40c14014b5da478cd05029ea
msgid "Physics models that will predict vehicle dynamics (attitude, velocity, positions,etc.) based on control inputs into the vehicle model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightaxis.rst:13
#: 24393c2d478f4119b3ae16441952c0e2
msgid "Graphics interpreter and display that takes the physics model's output and produces the graphics display of vehicle movement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightaxis.rst:15
#: 14c5207aed654c6aa415fd559b455372
msgid "A controller mechanism to produce control inputs into the physics model to command vehicle behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightaxis.rst:18
#: c0f285217588435d9da0bc5ddd68f6f9
msgid "In a normal RealFlight (RF) simulation, RF has built-in models, physics modeling, and graphic interpreter/display. Control is input via a simulation controller, such as the Interlink controller, joystick, or OpenTX transmitter in joystick mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightaxis.rst:20
#: ../../source/docs/flightaxis.rst:48
#: 31a49a1d32314ef3a4fdaf2a7e56ae61
#: 057a9343edb14b1d9df6d0247e200850
msgid "This is illustrated below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightaxis.rst:26
#: 3556aa5e97aa4acc9e05404203b3c726
msgid "The simulation controller outputs are mapped to \"TX channels\" by the RF controller editor to produce mapped RC outputs. For the InterLink controller these are fixed and read-only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightaxis.rst:28
#: 3d43d9a2c7f144d499d48626947fc521
msgid "They are input into the RealFlight vehicle model which is described by its .RFX file(archive actually). Most models have a \"software radio\" which take these \"TX channels\" and convert them into \"RX channels\", like a receiver. This \"software radio\" can also create dual rates, adjust trim, throw and reverses, etc. These received channels then drive motors, servos, or flight controller/mixers setup in the model files which drive the vehicle's actuators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightaxis.rst:30
#: 3eb357a40f7d4e198b589a323472047f
msgid "The Physics models takes these inputs, including the vehicles described physical characteristics from the model's files and predicts the vehicle's motion which is then graphically displayed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightaxis.rst:32
#: 36408b4e7ce044d4a650942eab030ed9
msgid "The pilot provides the \"autopilot\" function of inputing stick/switch control via the simulator controller to direct vehicle desired behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightaxis.rst:34
#: c8ba0b1e040841a287fd95944f71854c
msgid "An illustration of what constitutes a RealFlight model is show below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightaxis.rst:41
#: 181cbae4c413430aa5bd20201c41177f
msgid "SITL Using the FlightAxis Interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightaxis.rst:44
#: 27ec86e065ff4e838c7d7ef784acbd41
msgid "Using SITL to run the ArduPilot software basically is inserting an autopilot between the simulation controller and the vehicle, just like in real flight. This is done by tying a running SITL simulation  into RealFlight and using its Physics models and Graphics for the simulation. The interface between SITL and RealFlight is called FlightAxis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightaxis.rst:46
#: f751e4b247c94cc9b4236fe8e651a312
msgid "When enabled in RealFlight, it exports the vehicle's predicted attitude, velocities, position to SITL, as well as the outputs of the software radio of the vehicle model its using. SITL uses these as RC and sensor inputs in its sim and outputs servo functions  to RealFlight which it now interprets as the RX channel radio outputs used by the model for its actuator inputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightaxis.rst:53
#: d7c4b22723ee400088367bafcba78cb5
msgid "This basically inserts ArduPilot SITL simulation of the firmware between the pilot and RealFlights inputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightaxis.rst:55
#: 0b37b3fdfd5a4264925f42b19ec22f89
msgid "Presently, FlightAxis can transfer the first 12 RX channels from RealFlight to SITL RC inputs, and the first 12 SERVO outputs from SITL to RealFlights RX channel inputs."
msgstr ""
